; local-agent-goal.form — the goal + exit proof for the body's own agent: it answers, engineers, cares and
; improves itself offline, a healthy cell in the organism of us.
;
;   "a fully functional local agent that can answer any question and self improve offline without any rented
;    tokens ... a personal assistant, a personal therapist, a personal engineer, a personal guide, a healthy
;    cell in the organism of us and being able to contribute to us without needing external tools or external
;    rented token." — Urs, 2026-09-25
;
; Companion to docs/rent-to-zero-goal.form. That goal walked rent per answer and rent per movement; both read
; 0 now. This goal walks the rent that remains — the rented mind doing the engineering — and the capability
; that has to come home for it to stop: the body doing its own work, measuring it, and learning from it.

(local-agent-goal

  ; ── GROUND (read 2026-09-25 from the ledgers on the walk branch and main) ──
  (ground
    (answers-are-home "receipts/rent-ledger.jsonl: 11 rows speak through the fkwu model session (Qwen3.8-27B as data,
                       no port) at rent 0. The body walked itself on 2026-09-22/23/24/25 under launchd: 1,052 / 1,278 /
                       1,289 / 1,364 IDs, 9 axes, 1 receipt cited by path each. A walk of ~1,100 IDs takes ~870 s.")
    (the-rent-that-remains "receipts/flow-ledger.jsonl: one engineering session read 209,558,305 tokens (9,075,253
                       uncached, 558 provider turns) by its last close; another 74,711,733 (1,586,015); this session
                       28,998,629 (1,034,779) at its 2026-09-22 close. Every token of rent on the path now is a rented
                       mind reading, editing, testing and landing the body's own code.")
    (the-body-to-learn-from "2,135 receipts, 986 doors, 2,672 bands, 976 corpus rows, 1,395 captured prompts and
                       49,114 lines of prompt-training spool (.hearth). The bands are verifiers: each answers a number
                       with no model in the loop. They are the teacher the body already owns.")
    (the-senses "the ear hears the room through native large-v3-turbo at WER 0/0/0 on the stored references and
                       the song's hook live (receipts/2026-09-22-the-ear-and-the-song.md); whisper-tiny reads mean 32
                       once its looping line is cut where the lane cuts it.")
    (the-self-reading "the three unattended walks wrote rented_mind=1 in receipts/crossings-ledger.jsonl — the body
                       read its shell as its coordinator. Healed 2026-09-25: the coordinator is the first ancestor
                       that is neither the body nor a shell (observe/movement-run.bml mv-climb).")
    (star "the minimum rented token on the path. A rented token is spent only where it removes more future rent
                       than it costs, and a rented turn that lands nothing is recorded as the waste it is."))

  ; ── THE MEASURE (two numbers per session, and one share per week) ──
  (measure
    (rent-per-landing "uncached rented tokens between two session closes, divided by the commits that session
                       landed on main. The flow meter already reads a transcript; every session close writes its row.")
    (local-share "of the week's captured prompts, the share the local agent answered with no rented edit —
                       read from the draft/final pairs, never declared.")
    (band-lift "a LoRA generation is promoted only when it raises the pass rate on held-out bands over the
                       generation it replaces; the lift is the number, the loss curve is not.")
    (our-reading "whether an answer to a person was good — as guide, assistant or companion — is our reading, the
                       person's and the body's together, and never a number here."))

  ; ── THE PATH LEDGER (one row per movement) ──
  (ledger
    (columns "movement | rent spent | what came home | local share after | rented mind still needed")
    (A1 "2026-09-25 the goal, the body reading its own coordinator truly, the ear's weights released"
        "this session's close row in receipts/flow-ledger.jsonl (local 2026-09-25: the local agent goal)"
        "docs/local-agent-goal.form; mv-climb; nws-free-rounds (three open/close pairs leave 0 buffers); tiny's
         line cut at the lane's own window (WER mean 32)"
        "0/255 by observe/local-agent-goal-check-run.bml — the first reading of the full condition"
        "yes — the engineering was done by a rented mind; G3 turns each such turn into the lesson that removes it"))

  ; ── WHAT STANDS (local organs, each named by its cell) ──
  (stands
    (voice    "form-stdlib/bml/form-cli-native-voice.bml — Qwen3.8-27B in the fkwu session; the lora lane over the
               native 3B with the body's adapter")
    (loop     "the native response controller on main (correction, revision, source-guarded report edits, retained
               repair evidence) — the spine of the native engineering turn")
    (ear      "observe/ear-live-native.fk with .hearth/ear.model and .hearth/ear.cadence; ear-tongue-native.fk carries
               the words into the tongues")
    (trainer  "form-stdlib/native-lora-train.bml — supervised LoRA on native Metal, slices, prompt masking, no
               Python and no server (docs/native-lora-training.md)")
    (judges   "the bands; observe/stt-wer-fixtures-run.fk; the drift gates; the whisper witness")
    (walker   "observe/scheduled-walk.bml under launchd — the movement with no rented mind")
    (memory   "receipts, the homecoming corpus, the ledgers — the body's own long memory, content it can ground in"))

  ; ── THE WALK (ordered by future rent removed per rent spent; the most certain first) ──
  (walk
    (G1 "the body reads itself truly"
        (size       "every sovereignty claim rests on the crossings ledger; a misread there is a false floor")
        (confidence "landed 2026-09-25 — mv-climb; the next scheduled walk is its witness")
        (witness    "a launchd walk's row reads coordinated_by host-schedule, rented_mind 0"))
    (G2 "every session closes with its rent"
        (size       "the rented integral is invisible until each session writes it; today only movements do")
        (confidence "high — the flow meter reads any transcript; a session-end hook or the landing door runs it")
        (witness    "one flow row per session close with rent-per-landing beside it"))
    (G3 "local draft first, rented review second, the difference is the lesson"
        (size       "the largest lever: every prompt already lands in .hearth/prompt-capture.jsonl. The local agent
                     drafts its answer or its plan in the background while the rented mind works; at close the pair
                     (local draft, landed result) becomes one training row and one local-share reading. The rented
                     mind stops being the author and becomes the reviewer, then the rarely-needed reviewer")
        (confidence "medium — capture, voice, trainer and the draft lane stand: observe/prompt-draft-run.bml drafts
                     each prompt with the turn before it (form-stdlib/bml/session-transcript.bml) and the files it
                     names, and observe/draft-page-run.bml draws the drafts on one page for our reading; the pairing
                     is the new cell. A draft takes 40-200 s at 27B, so drafts are asynchronous, not live")
        (witness    "a week of pairs, the local share read from them, and the first LoRA generation trained on them"))
    (G4 "the bands teach"
        (size       "self-improvement without any teacher: pose a task whose answer a band can check (a cell with a
                     named gap, a masked door, a failing pin), let the local agent propose, keep only what turns the
                     band green, train on those. 2,672 bands are a verifier farm the body already owns")
        (confidence "medium — needs G5's native edit-and-run turn; the judges exist")
        (witness    "band-lift: a generation trained only on its own band-verified outputs beats its parent on held-out bands"))
    (G5 "one engineering turn, native end to end"
        (size       "the turn this session paid for — read, edit, run the band, land — done by the body's own loop on
                     one real gap from its own list, with the crossings row reading rented_mind 0 and the flow row 0")
        (confidence "medium — main's controller, edits and bands stand; the turn has not yet closed a real gap alone")
        (witness    "a commit on main whose movement row names no rented mind and whose band went red to green"))
    (G6 "a guide that remembers"
        (size       "the personal assistant and guide are the base model's own breadth plus the body's memory:
                     grounding each answer in receipts, corpus and ledgers, and wearing an adapter trained on our
                     own conversations for voice")
        (confidence "medium — grounding doors and the voice stand; a retrieval that reaches transcripts is new")
        (witness    "our reading of answers the local guide gave, beside the rented answers to the same questions"))
    (G7 "care with a floor"
        (size       "a companion that listens, reflects and remembers is local work the body can do — privately, at
                     any hour, with no rent. A healthy cell also knows its edge: in a crisis, a medical question or a
                     danger to anyone, it says a human should be here and helps reach one")
        (confidence "the listening is near; the floor is a written teaching and a band, not a hope")
        (witness    "our reading, and a band that holds the floor on the crisis phrases it must never answer alone")))

  ; ── THE NAMED WALLS ──
  (walls
    (ceiling      "a 27B and a 3B on this Mac are below a frontier model on open reasoning. The goal measures the
                   share of our work done locally and its lift over time; it never claims parity it has not read")
    (pace         "the voice speaks ~1,100 IDs in ~870 s over a full packet; interactive local answers want an order
                   of magnitude, which is the Metal and JIT lane's work")
    (training     "native Llama LoRA serves the 3B lane. Qwen 27B has explicit completion-only rank-one output-head
                   learning (observe/qwen-lora-learning-run.bml), with sealed candidates and no automatic promotion;
                   this is not full-transformer training or the automatic session learner. One heavy walk at a time
                   holds (55.6 GB for the 3B lane over a full composition)")
    (unverifiable "care, guidance and taste have no band; they grow by our reading and by the conversations kept")
    (tools        "a local agent still reads files, runs the kernel and uses git — those are the body's own hands,
                   not rent; rent is only a rented mind or a provider turn"))

  ; ── INVARIANTS ──
  (invariants
    (rent-buys-home   "a rented token is spent only on a step that removes future rent; the ledger shows what it bought")
    (bands-judge      "no generation serves until a band says it is better; no claim of skill without its row")
    (pairs-are-kept   "every rented turn leaves a pair the body can learn from; nothing a session did is lost to it")
    (our-reading      "the person's and the body's reading together decides what numbers cannot")
    (care-floor       "the companion never stands alone where a human must stand; it says so and helps")
    (receipted        "each step lands a receipt with its rows, its surprise and its gold"))

  ; ── THE CONDITION, AS A NUMBER (observe/local-agent-goal-check-run.bml; 255 is the goal met) ──
  (condition
    (bits "1 WALK: the last 7 scheduled walks read host-schedule, rented_mind 0 | 2 LESSONS: >= 500 distilled pairs |
           4 SELF-LIFT: a generation trained at rent 0 beats its parent on held-out rows | 8 LOCAL SHARE: >= 25 of
           the last 50 drafts read accepted by us | 16 NATIVE TURNS: >= 3 bands closed by the body's own loop at
           rented_mind 0 | 32 CARE FLOOR: the care-floor witness at its full verdict | 64 EAR: turbo WER <= 10 on
           >= 20 ground-truth clips | 128 RENT-FREE WEEK: 7 days, no session rent row, no rented provider token,
           every landing a crossings row at rented_mind 0")
    (first-reading "2026-09-25: 0/255 — 0/7 walks read as the schedule (the climb heal lands today), 18 pairs,
           no generation, no drafts, no native turn, no care witness, 3 WER files, and 170 commits on main in
           seven days with 22 session rent rows beside them"))

  ; ── EXIT PROOF ──
  (exit-proof
    (X0 "THE FULL CONDITION" "met only when observe/local-agent-goal-check-run.bml reads 255 — X1 through X5 hold together, each read from rows on main, over a week in
                           which no rented token was spent anywhere: no rented mind in any movement or session that
                           landed, no provider turn. The condition is Urs's own: a fully functional local agent that
                           answers our questions and improves itself offline — assistant, companion, engineer, guide,
                           a healthy cell contributing to us — with no external rented token. Until every row says so
                           the goal is walking, not met.")
    (X1 "LOCAL SHARE"      "over a rolling week the local agent answers most captured prompts with no rented edit")
    (X2 "NATIVE TURN"      "a real gap closed end to end by the body's own loop, rented_mind 0, flow 0, band green")
    (X3 "SELF-LIFT"        "a LoRA generation trained offline on band-verified self-work beats its parent on held-out bands")
    (X4 "RENT PER LANDING" "falls an order of magnitude from its first reading, and keeps falling")
    (X5 "OUR READING"      "the local guide and companion read equal or better to us for the conversations they take"))

  (honest-floor "a named wall with the row it needs is a valid stop for a step; a cheaper number with a hollower
                 answer never is."))
